  "learn": {
    "title": "Connected Greenhouse",
    "body": "Wire BME280 VIN to 3V3, GND to GND, SDA to GPIO21 and SCL to GPIO22. Wire servo signal to GPIO18, power to VIN (5 V), and GND to GND. Wire GPIO23 → 220 Ω → LED → GND; it indicates an open vent. Join virtual VoltNet with password pass and broker.voltquest.local:1883.\n\nStart in AUTO with the vent closed at 30°. Sample every 100 ms. In AUTO open to 150° at 30°C or above, close at 27°C or below, and retain the previous state in between. Subscribe to greenhouse/mode: OPEN and CLOSE override temperature; AUTO restores hysteresis. Reject other payloads with INVALID on greenhouse/error while retaining the mode. Acknowledge valid modes on greenhouse/mode/state. Publish greenhouse/status every 500 ms and serve GET /status with the same live text: mode=AUTO;temp=33.0;vent=OPEN. Apply the servo and LED together.\n\nRun at the default temperature. Set 33°C and observe AUTO opening. Publish CLOSE and keep it closed despite the heat. Publish BAD and verify INVALID without a mode change. Publish AUTO to reopen, then lower the sensor to 26°C and request /status: mode=AUTO;temp=26.0;vent=CLOSED. This virtual vent models commanded angle, not greenhouse airflow or servo load.",
    "links": []
  },
